// Smartflow Autobase Surface Generation — Phá thử, regression và chặn lỗi tái phát
// ROLE: REGRESSION_STRESS - long-run / adversarial behaviour of an existing capability.
//
// Purpose: create flat base surface from destination UV geometry
// Algorithm under stress: Canonical shapes/curves via Rust domain + OCCT FFI; never treat renderer tessellation or viewport cache as authoritative BRep. Use documented source/target frames; mm model units; numeric and topology tolerances from approved G00, not guessed values. EntityId/FeatureId/LayerId/InstanceId & provenance stable; preserve non-selected entities, layer locks and instance semantics. Preview read-only against committed model; Cancel same document hash; one Commit equals one atomic Undo transaction; error rolls back. History dependency directed acyclic graph, serializable stable parameter schema, deterministic recompute, no silent source detach. MVP golden fixtures and existing M07 STL/cutters must not regress after E13. Base/destination UV directions, normal/winding, trimmed boundaries, periodic seams and rigid gem placement explicitly validated. Generate base corresponding to selected surface; assert unambiguous UV orientation and mapped corners. None
//
// Loop skeleton (choose the parameters from the fixture, then record them):
//   for round in 0..N {
//       apply the same operation to an increasingly large/pathological input
//       measure: wall time, allocation, handle/leak count, geometry drift vs tolerance
//       stop criterion: <max rounds> or <drift > tolerance> or <first failure>
//   }
//
// Assertions:
//   - results stay within the declared tolerance for every round
//   - no leaked OCCT/GPU resource: create/destroy counts balance
//   - the first failing round is reported with its input, not summarised away
// Positive oracle: Generate base corresponding to selected surface; assert unambiguous UV orientation and mapped corners
// Negative oracle: Empty/wrong type selection; document locked, missing asset/feature ID, stale reference.
